# Backend Style

Every JS file must mirror the reference project's layer for its role.

## Layering (copy this shape)

| Role | Reference example | This repo |
|---|---|---|
| Route handler | `app/api/session/create/route.ts` | inside `app.js` |
| Service (business logic) | `services/sessionService.ts` | `services/<feature>Service.js` |
| DAO (DB only) | `services/dao/sessionDao.ts` | `services/dao/<feature>Dao.js` |
| Pure helpers (no I/O) | `lib/trial.ts`, `lib/utils.ts` | `lib/<feature>.js` |
| Barrel | `services/index.ts` | `services/index.js` |

## Naming

- Service verbs: `createX`, `saveX`, `getX`, `endX`, `claimX`, `ensureX`.
- DAO verbs: `insertX`, `fetchX`, `updateX`, `countX`.
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` at the top of the module.
- File-private helpers: `_camelCase` at the bottom of the module.

## Route handler shape (mirror `app/api/session/create/route.ts`)

```js
app.post("/thing", async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const userId = req.body?.userId
    if (!userId || typeof userId !== "string") {
      return res.status(400).json({ error: "userId (string) is required" })
    }
    try {
      const result = await featureService.doThing(pool, userId, req.body)
      return res.json({ success: true, ...result })
    } catch (e) {
      return res.status(400).json({ error: e instanceof Error ? e.message : "Invalid payload" })
    }
  } catch (e) {
    console.error("[API thing]", e)
    return res.status(500).json({ error: e instanceof Error ? e.message : "Failed" })
  }
})
```

